cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use te-drift-detector in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "te-drift-detector: experimental lexical feature-delta telemetry"
abstract: >-
  Experimental lexical feature-delta telemetry for multi-turn text. This
  standard-library Python package extracts lexical features, compares them with
  a first-turn baseline, and reports raw deltas and uncalibrated heuristic
  threshold crossings for human inspection. Its bundled synthetic fixtures are
  implementation self-checks, not evidence of detection efficacy or safety
  severity.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Hermes Labs"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-08-04"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hermes-labs-ai/te-drift-detector"
keywords:
  - large-language-models
  - agents
  - drift-detection
  - multi-turn
  - evaluation
  - monitoring
